/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 141 0 R
/T (The fund targets a total size of CHF 500,000, with CHF 200,000 already raised from the GP team and close LP network. The remaining CHF 300,000 is expected from 7 to 10 investment committee investors, each contributing approximately CHF 30,000 to CHF 50,000. TechAir plans to invest in four to five validated early-stage startups, with ticket sizes of CHF 75,000 to CHF 100,000, primarily through post-money SAFEs. This concentrated portfolio allows the fund to provide meaningful financial and strategic support to each company while keeping the investment structure simple and founder-friendly.)
/E (The fund targets a total size of CHF 500,000, with CHF 200,000 already raised from the GP team and close LP network. The remaining CHF 300,000 is expected from 7 to 10 investment committee investors, each contributing approximately CHF 30,000 to CHF 50,000. TechAir plans to invest in four to five validated early-stage startups, with ticket sizes of CHF 75,000 to CHF 100,000, primarily through post-money SAFEs. This concentrated portfolio allows the fund to provide meaningful financial and strategic support to each company while keeping the investment structure simple and founder-friendly.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
244 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 141 0 R
/T (TechAir Venture is a student-run impact investment fund focused on early-stage decarbonization deeptech startups. The fund aims to finance technologies that reduce, avoid, or capture greenhouse gas emissions by providing solutions in energy efficiency, carbon capture, and alternative fuels. These solutions are targeted at high-emission sectors such as energy, materials, buildings, transport, and industrial processes, where decarbonization needs are the most urgent.)
/E (TechAir Venture is a student-run impact investment fund focused on early-stage decarbonization deeptech startups. The fund aims to finance technologies that reduce, avoid, or capture greenhouse gas emissions by providing solutions in energy efficiency, carbon capture, and alternative fuels. These solutions are targeted at high-emission sectors such as energy, materials, buildings, transport, and industrial processes, where decarbonization needs are the most urgent.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
