1821 0 obj
<<
/Title (To mitigate these risks, TechAir invests only in startups with initial EPFL-linked validation, such as a lab connection, grant, accelerator program, spin-off status, proof of concept, prototype, or early pilot. Each investment is assessed through financial, technical, and impact due diligence, focusing on market need, technological credibility, capital requirements, and measurable decarbonization potential.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1795 0 R
/Prev 1809 0 R
/Next 1810 0 R
>>
endobj
1822 0 obj
<<
/Title (We propose a 1% annual management fee on committed capital, used only for legal costs, due diligence, reporting, and impact measurement.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1812 0 R
>>
endobj
1823 0 obj
<<
/Title (We focus on decarbonization solutions in energy efficiency, carbon capture, and alternative fuels, targeting high-emission sectors such as energy systems, materials, buildings, transport, and industrial processes where deeptech can create meaningful climate impact.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1815 0 R
>>
endobj
1824 0 obj
<<
/Title (Impact and Commercial Alignment)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1793 0 R
/Prev 1815 0 R
/First 1829 0 R
/Last 1829 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 1816 0 R
>>
endobj
1825 0 obj
<<
/Title (Our thesis is that regulatory pressure, corporate climate commitments, and consumer demand will increase the need for scalable decarbonization solutions. We focus on startups whose core technology can deliver measurable emissions reduction while building commercially viable products.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1816 0 R
>>
endobj
1826 0 obj
<<
/Title (TechAir Ventures invests in validated early-stage decarbonization deeptech startups, mainly at the pre-seed and seed stage. Target companies should have a clear link to the EPFL ecosystem, through a lab, grant, accelerator, research program, spin-off status, or other form of technical or entrepreneurial validation.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1819 0 R
>>
endobj
1827 0 obj
